ew" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>BESSHO MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATTORI TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BESSHO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATTORI, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBAKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A device for decomposing an organic halogen compound in a thermal plasma which is produced by irradiating with a microwave a gas containing an organic halogen compound, wherein a mist separator for separating and removing oil components mixed in the organic halogen compound is disposed downstream a cylinder storing therein the organic halogen compound to thereby prevent pipeline contamination and production of by-products. The cylinder is immersed in a hot water in a temperature-controlled tank and a saturated steam temperature in the cylinder is kept constant to thereby keep a jetting pressure constant, minimize variations in volumetric flow rate of the organic halogen compound, and stabilize plasma continuously over an extended time.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de décomposition d'un composé halogène organique, dans un plasma thermique que l'on produit en soumettant à un rayonnement d'ondes hyperfréquences un gaz contenant un composé halogène organique. Ce dispositif comprend un séparateur de brouillard destiné à séparer et éliminer les constituants huileux mélangés avec le composé halogène organique, ce séparateur étant placé en aval d'un cylindre de stockage du composé halogène organique, de manière à empêcher la contamination du pipeline et la production de sous-produits. On immerge ledit cylindre dans de l'eau chaude, dans une cuve à température régulée et on maintient constante une température de vapeur saturée dans le cylindre, afin de conserver une pression constante de giclement, de minimiser des variations dans le débit volumétrique du composé halogène organique et de stabiliser le plasma de manière continue sur une période prolongée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>